= Reputation system — Technical =

A reputation mechanism specifies an event/feedback model, identity model, aggregation rule, time weighting, context transfer policy, visibility rule, and attack model. Robust design must consider strategic reporting, sparse data, correlated raters, Sybil identities, whitewashing, cold start, and uncertainty in the estimate.

== Modeling cautions ==
* reputation ≠ identity
* reputation ≠ trust by definition
* high score ≠ verified future behavior

== References ==
* Paul Resnick, Richard Zeckhauser, Eric Friedman & Ko Kuwabara, “Reputation Systems” (''Communications of the ACM'', 2000).
* Chrysanthos Dellarocas, “The Digitization of Word of Mouth” (2003).
* distributed-systems and online-marketplace literature on reputation and strategic manipulation.
